## 4️⃣ ORGANIZER LOGIN

**POST**
`/api/auth/login`

**Body:**
```json
{
  "email": "organizer@gmail.com",
  "password": "12345678"
}
```

---

## 5️⃣ ADMIN LOGIN

**POST**
`/api/auth/login`

**Body:**
```json
{
  "email": "admin@gmail.com",
  "password": "ADMIN_PASSWORD"
}
```

Admin ka role backend/database mein `admin` hona chahiye.

**Response:**
```json
{
  "message": "Login successful",
  "user": {
    "id": "...",
    "name": "Admin",
    "email": "admin@gmail.com",
    "role": "admin"
  },
  "accessToken": "..."
}
```

---

### 🔑 Authorization

Protected APIs ke liye header:

`Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`

# Event Management System — App API Guide

This document explains how the frontend communicates with the Node.js backend and uses the ML-integrated APIs.

## 1. Architecture

```text
Frontend
   |
   | HTTP Requests
   v
Node.js / Express Backend
   |
   | Axios
   v
ML / FastAPI Service
```

The frontend should communicate **only with the Node.js backend**.

The frontend should **not directly call the ML/FastAPI service**.

---

## 2. Backend Base URL

### Local Development

```text
http://localhost:8000
```

API base:

```text
http://localhost:8000/api/v1
```

Example:

```text
http://localhost:8000/api/v1/ml/student/recommend
```

---

## 3. Authentication

Protected APIs require the access token in the request header:

```http
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN>
```

Example:

```js
const response = await fetch(
  "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/ml/student/recommend",
  {
    method: "POST",
    headers: {
      "Content-Type": "application/json",
      "Authorization": `Bearer ${token}`
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(data)
  }
);
```

Do not send MongoDB credentials, JWT secrets, or ML service credentials from the frontend.

---

## 4. User Roles

The backend supports:

```text
USER
ORGANIZER
ADMIN
```

ML APIs are protected according to these roles.

---

# 5. ML API Endpoints

## 5.1 Student Recommendations

### Endpoint

```http
POST /api/v1/ml/student/recommend
```

### Role

```text
USER
```

### Request Body

```json
{
  "domain": "Technology",
  "skills": "Python, Machine Learning",
  "year": "2",
  "branch": "CSE",
  "mode": "Any",
  "top_n": 5
}
```

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "recommendations": [
      {
        "title": "AI Hackathon",
        "organization": "ABC Organization",
        "domain": "Technology",
        "category": "Hackathon",
        "mode": "Online",
        "deadline": "2026-10-20",
        "required_skills": "Python, Machine Learning",
        "application_url": "https://example.com",
        "score": 0.91,
        "matched": "Python, Machine Learning",
        "missing": ""
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Use this API on the student dashboard to display personalized opportunities.

---

# 6. Organizer APIs

## 6.1 Predict Event Registrations

### Endpoint

```http
POST /api/v1/ml/organizer/predict-registrations
```

### Role

```text
ORGANIZER
```

### Request Body

```json
{
  "domain": "Technology",
  "category": "Hackathon",
  "mode": "Online",
  "prize_money_inr": 50000,
  "application_fee_inr": 0,
  "certificate_available": 1,
  "duration_days": 3,
  "deadline_to_start_days": 15,
  "stipend_inr": 0,
  "team_required": 1
}
```

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "predicted_registrations": 1234
  }
}
```

Use this while creating or editing an event.

---

## 6.2 Event Demand

### Endpoint

```http
GET /api/v1/ml/organizer/event-demand
```

### Role

```text
ORGANIZER
```

No request body is required.

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "total_events": 10,
    "event_status": {
      "pending": 3,
      "approved": 6,
      "rejected": 1
    },
    "mode_distribution": {
      "online": 5,
      "offline": 3,
      "hybrid": 2
    }
  }
}
```

Use this for organizer dashboard charts and statistics.

---

## 6.3 Organizer Analytics

### Endpoint

```http
GET /api/v1/ml/organizer/analytics
```

### Role

```text
ORGANIZER
```

No request body is required.

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "platform_statistics": {
      "total_users": 100,
      "total_organizers": 20,
      "total_events": 50
    },
    "organizer_statistics": {
      "pending_verification": 5,
      "verified": 15
    },
    "event_statistics": {
      "pending": 10,
      "approved": 35,
      "rejected": 5
    }
  }
}
```

Use this on the organizer analytics/dashboard page.

---

# 7. Admin Event Risk Detection

### Endpoint

```http
POST /api/v1/ml/admin/event-risk
```

### Role

```text
ADMIN
```

### Request Body

```json
{
  "popularity_score": 75,
  "registration_count": 1200,
  "synthetic_views": 5000,
  "prize_money_inr": 50000,
  "application_fee_inr": 0,
  "stipend_inr": 0,
  "duration_days": 2,
  "deadline_to_start_days": 10,
  "certificate_available": 1,
  "team_required": 1,
  "team_size_fixed": 4,
  "mode_fixed": 1,
  "prize_category_conflict": 0,
  "stipend_category_conflict": 0
}
```

### Response

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "admin_status": "NORMAL",
    "risk_score": 32.45,
    "review_priority": "LOW",
    "anomaly_score": 0.1755
  }
}
```

Use this in the admin dashboard to display event risk information.

